# 9. Technology Stack

[tabs]
[tab title="Ingestion"]
[table cols="Component,Technology,Purpose"
  Event SDK          | Custom JS/iOS/Android | Client-side event capture
  API Gateway        | Kong                  | Rate limiting, auth, routing
  Message Broker     | Apache Kafka          | Durable event streaming
  Schema Registry    | Confluent SR (Avro)   | Schema enforcement and evolution
]
[/tab]
[tab title="Processing"]
[table cols="Component,Technology,Purpose"
  Stream Processing  | Apache Flink 1.18     | Real-time metrics and validation
  Batch Processing   | Apache Spark 3.5      | Historical aggregation and ETL
  Orchestration      | Apache Airflow        | DAG scheduling for batch jobs
  Transformation     | dbt                   | Business-layer SQL models
]
[/tab]
[tab title="Storage"]
[table cols="Component,Technology,Purpose"
  Raw Data Lake      | S3 / GCS (Parquet)    | Immutable event archive
  OLAP Store         | Apache Druid          | Sub-second real-time queries
  Live Counters      | Redis Cluster         | Real-time metric serving
  Data Warehouse     | Snowflake / BigQuery  | Historical analytics and BI
  Feature Store      | Feast + Tecton        | ML feature serving and training
]
[/tab]
[tab title="Dashboards & Alerts"]
[table cols="Component,Technology,Purpose"
  Engineering Board  | Grafana               | Pipeline health, infra metrics
  BI Dashboard       | Tableau / Superset    | Business KPIs and reporting
  Alerting           | PagerDuty + Slack     | Incident and quality alerts
  Data Quality       | Great Expectations    | Rule-based data validation
  Tracing            | OpenTelemetry + Jaeger | Distributed pipeline tracing
]
[/tab]
[/tabs]

[divider]

# 10. Scalability & SLA Summary

[columns]
[col]
[section title="Throughput Targets" style=card]
[kpi label="Daily Events" value="2B+" target="2B" trend=+5% color=blue]
[kpi label="Peak Throughput" value="28K/sec" target="30K/sec" trend=+8% color=green]
[kpi label="Stream End-to-End" value="<500ms" target="<500ms" trend=0% color=green]
[kpi label="Batch SLA" value="<30min" target="<30min" trend=-5% color=green]
[/section]
[/col]
[col]
[section title="Reliability Targets" style=card]
[kpi label="Ingestion Uptime" value="99.99%" target="99.99%" trend=0% color=green]
[kpi label="Data Completeness" value=">99.9%" target="99.9%" trend=+0.02% color=green]
[kpi label="DLQ Rate" value="<0.1%" target="<0.1%" trend=-0.02% color=green]
[kpi label="Feature Freshness SLA" value="99.7%" target="99.5%" trend=+0.2% color=green]
[/section]
[/col]
[/columns]

[section title="Key Design Decisions" style=card]
[list style=numbered]
- **Lambda Architecture** — Flink for speed layer (real-time), Spark for batch layer (accuracy), Druid/DW as serving layer satisfies both latency and historical query needs
- **Schema Registry with Avro** — Enforces schema evolution contracts at ingestion time, preventing downstream breakage from producer changes
- **DLQ-first validation** — Invalid events are never silently dropped; they're routed to `dlq.events` for replay after fixes, ensuring no data loss
- **Feature freshness gating** — Model promotion in CI/CD is blocked if any feature group breaches its freshness SLA, preventing stale-feature degradation in production
- **Tiered alerting (P1/P2/P3)** — Reduces alert fatigue by separating actionable outages (P1) from quality degradation (P2) and monitoring anomalies (P3)
[/list]
[/section]

[callout icon=🚀 title="Next Steps" text="Phase 1: Deploy Kafka + Flink stream pipeline with validation. Phase 2: Build Spark batch ETL and DW models. Phase 3: Launch BI + Grafana dashboards. Phase 4: Integrate Feature Store with ML model CI/CD." color=blue]
